WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm very happy
to have you here.

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's very nice
to have you in New York.

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
You and I have
an opposite situation.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
I live in New York.
My brother lives in L.A.

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:07.440
You live in L.A.
Your brother lives in New York.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:07.907 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.109 size:78% position:39%
-Do you get a chance
to hang out with him?

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:10.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I get a chance
every time I come to New York.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:14.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
This time around, I missed him
cause he's traveling, so...

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.582
-Okay.
-So, this time around, I didn't.

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:16.383 line:92%
-Does he take it personally

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.585
that you just chose to come
when he was on the road?

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:19.219 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.920
-I don't know about that, but...
-[ Laughing ] Okay, yeah.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But it's always nice
to see him.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:25.258
Always, when I come to New York,
it's like --

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:26.192 size:84% position:42% line:92%
we always go out and...

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.328
-Does he sort of know how to --
how to treat you

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:30.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the best of the city
when you're here?

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's a connoisseur
of pizza restaurants.

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:34.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's good.
-You know? And...

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's the right kind
of connoisseur to be around.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.338
-Yeah, you know, and a --
and a good steak, too.

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.407
You know?
-Okay, are you picky with pizza?

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.542
'Cause people always ask me
what my favorite pizza is,

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:45.779
and I have to say, "All pizza."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:47.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, there's --
there's really good pizza.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And then there's all pizza.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:51.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I think that's fair.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
There's no, like, bad --

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:53.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
I -- I mean --
-Well...

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah,
there's some bad pizza, yeah.

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:56.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In L.A.,
there's some bad pizza, yeah.

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:57.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:57.357 --> 00:01:00.927
-I'm so excited that
there is a sequel to "Sicario,"

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was a movie
from a couple years ago

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:03.696 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that I absolutely loved.

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:06.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you surprised
that this came back around

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.968 line:92%
to tell more of this story?

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.637 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah, a little bit.

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:11.171 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:14.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, the -- the --
the first --

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:17.610
the first movie was, I thought,
a good movie,

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:23.116
and so it had a great group
of filmmakers working on it.

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:26.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
So when they decided to do
this one,

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:26.986 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I was a little skeptical

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:29.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we were going to have
a new director...

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:30.256 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...a new
director of photography, so...

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:37.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the story that the writer
wrote, Taylor Sheridan,

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:40.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
was very original
and unpredictable

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:43.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
and had a lot of those, like,
"Oh [bleep]" moments...

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...that -- that --

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I felt when I --
when I read it, I felt like,

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, you know what?
Let's tackle it."

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:49.876 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-That's very exciting.

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:51.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you must have felt
the character --

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:54.814
the character you played was
so wonderful in the first film.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you feel like it changed
to a place

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:58.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be interesting
to take it on again?

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:01.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I think
he evolves quite a bit

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.890 size:75% position:38% line:92%
in -- in this story,

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the new
"Sicario: Day of the Soldado."

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:08.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
He kind of like --
I like to say he --

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:09.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, in the first one,
we meet him,

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:10.530 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and he's like a hit man

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:16.136
and a heartless, one-track mind
kind of guy bent on revenge.

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:18.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
And in this one,
I think that --

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:23.309
It's through his journey,
I think, we find out that he --

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.011 line:92%
he's rehabilitated to an extent.

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:28.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's not innocent,
but he's rehabilitated

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
through this relationship
that he has

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:32.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
with this young girl
called Isabela

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
played by Isabela Moner.
Yeah.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.755 size:88% position:44%
-That's really exciting.
I can't wait to see it.

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.557 size:81% position:41%
I've -- Like I said,
I loved the first one.

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:39.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also want to ask,
in recent years,

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:44.264
"Guardians of the Galaxy,"
"Avengers," "Star Wars" --

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:46.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
are those exciting movies
to be a part of?

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:47.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were those
the kind of movies that,

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you were a kid,
you would have enjoyed?

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:50.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. What do you -- Yeah.
-[ Chuckling ] Yeah.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, that's the way I feel.
Yeah.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
-Big time. Big time.

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:56.910
It's like -- It's like
going back to the future.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:57.544 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:57.544 --> 00:03:02.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I'm very lucky that
"Star Wars" called.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:04.884
You know, the director
Rian Johnson on "The Last Jedi,"

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:07.320
he called me up,
and I said, "Yeah, no problem."

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.189 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And so did James Gunn,

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:11.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he called me up to play
The Collector

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:13.126 line:92%
in "Guardians of the Galaxy,"

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:15.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that's a --
you know, that's a --

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:16.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's an actor's dream.
-Yeah.

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:18.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know? Yeah.
-Just the call. Any call.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just any call. Any call.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.902
-Yeah. I remember, as an actor,
if your phone rings

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's not, like,
the bill collector,

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:25.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're like,
"This is a good day."

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-It's a good day, for sure.

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:30.643
-So, I know,
on probably all these projects,

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:33.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
scripts are like
tightly guarded secrets,

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:36.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
and for "Star Wars,"
is it true that

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
they had to bring a tablet
to your house,

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:40.253
and someone had to wait outside
while you read it?

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:43.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. They bring --
They bring, like, an iPad

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:46.926 size:78% position:39%
with -- with the code
and the whole bit,

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:47.794 line:92%
and the script is right there,

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:51.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was really --
I'm a slow reader, you know?

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:53.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.367 line:92%
-It -- You know, usually,

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:58.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
it could take me 8, 10 hours
to really read a script.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:03:59.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-I mean, I can read it.

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:01.307 size:78% position:39%
-I feel like you take
some breaks, yeah.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:02.875 line:92%
-Yeah, you know, of course I do.

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
I daydream quite a bit.
-Uh-huh.

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:06.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I digress.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:09.515 size:84% position:42%
But -- But, you know,
a "Star Wars" script --

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:12.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's -- it's got
a lot of weird names and...

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:12.852 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah, that makes sense.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:15.722
-...it's like a new language,
and so it took a long time.

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:17.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, that guy --
that poor guy was waiting

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:20.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
for, I'd say, about 8 hours.
-[ Laughing ] Yeah?

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:21.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. You know?

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you give him
a chair or anything?

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was he sitting in a car?
What was he doing?

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:26.165 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, um...

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:27.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
Uh, no, I didn't.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:29.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
I-I kind of forgot
that he was there.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, no, that's --

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:31.371 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's terrible.

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:33.306
They say that's one of
the side effects of daydreaming.

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:34.207 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:35.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You forget where you are
or who you are.

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:36.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
-Yeah.

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:38.544
-You have a --
You have a 7-year-old daughter.

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:40.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I do. Yeah.
-Does she --

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:41.147 line:92%
Are -- Are these movies --

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:42.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do they appeal to her,
your movies,

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:44.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
or what are the movies
she's into?

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:46.085 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Well, she really loves,

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:49.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, the --
the "Star Wars" --

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:51.557
she likes the "Star Wars" movie
that I've done.

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:54.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, of course, she's not
going to be able to see

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.094 line:92%
"Sicario: Day of the Soldado"

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the next 10 years.
-Right, yeah.

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:57.463 size:84% position:42%
Well, not until she saw
the first "Sicario,"

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.899
or else it won't make sense.
-Right, right. Exactly, yeah.

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:00.967 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:01.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Totally.
-Yeah.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:05.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you know what movie
she really loves?

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:11.377
And it -- She's a big fan
of Josh Brolin in "The Goonies."

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:13.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ooh, "Goonies." Sure.
-"Goonies." Yeah.

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:14.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:18.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it --
it's really funny 'cause...

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:20.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, has she met Josh?
-She hasn't.

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:22.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
-But -- But she will,

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:24.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
but she might be surprised
when she sees him.

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:25.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I don't think he's changed
that much.

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:28.194 size:78% position:39%
-Yeah, we actually --
we have side-by-sides

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:32.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
of -- of modern-day Brolin
and "Goonies" Brolin.

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:33.533 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:35.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, the same-sized skull,
you know?

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:37.236
-Yeah. He does have a big head.
-Big head.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
He does have a big head.
Yeah.

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.972 size:84% position:42%
-You've worked with him
up close and personal.

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:42.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've worked with him
on five projects.

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:42.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Five movies?
-Yeah.

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:45.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Two "Sicarios."
What are the -- What else?

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:48.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"The Avengers."
-Right. Of course.

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:50.850 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-"Inherent Vice"...

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:54.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
Paul Thomas Anderson
and with Joaquin Phoenix.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.488 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And what else did I do?

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:59.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did a TV show
early on in my career.

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:02.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was 20, probably,
and he was the lead --

00:06:02.095 --> 00:06:03.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was called "Private Eye."
-Okay.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:04.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I guest-starred on a TV show.
-Gotcha.

00:06:04.764 --> 00:06:05.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And he --
that's where I met him.

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:06.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's fant--
-So, yeah.

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:08.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And did --
And when you worked together,

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.103
'cause I guess then it was
probably at least a decade

00:06:10.103 --> 00:06:11.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
before
you worked together again,

00:06:11.104 --> 00:06:12.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
did he remember you
from "Private Eye"?

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:14.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I hope he did.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.309 line:92%
I never asked, but, yeah.

00:06:16.309 --> 00:06:18.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think he did.
I think he did, yeah.

